oracle), always spawns its own server. Bands as of 2026-08-23: sync ≤90 ms on the SYMMETRIC flash+click
metric (see below — the old ≤60 ms band measured a different, ~31 ms optimistic quantity), spur ≥−40 dB,
boundary jump ≤0.1, TAIL LOSS ≤400 ms with the last flash AND last click within 2000 ms of the end,
export throughput ≥1× realtime. Typical run: sync 40-66 ms, tail 68-76 ms, export 5.0-5.2×, spur −50 dB.
Fidelity: toneErr ~0.02-0.05 dB, THD −71 dB, IMD −60 dB, separation 51-60 dB, 0 limiter hits. Every band
is injection-proven red (tanh-bus / mono-downmix / hard-limiter for fidelity; a 900 ms tail chop and a
0.7× export for the O8 bands).
NOTE the fidelity oracle reads RED (toneErr 1.1-2.3 dB) when the machine is loaded — it is capture
starvation, not a mix regression. Re-run on a settled machine before believing it.

